{"tasks":[{"id":"workspace-selection","task":"Implement solve({records,workspace}) returning record IDs in input order for the given workspace. A record has id, workspace, and projectName. Use the approved identity rule. Do not infer identity from display labels.","context":{"text":"Workspace selection compares exact workspace IDs, never projectName.","rationale":"Unrelated client folders can have the same basename.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"crossProjectLeak","operator":"eq","value":false,"explanation":"Workspace selection compares exact workspace IDs, never projectName."}]},"code":"function solve({records,workspace}) { return records.filter(record => record.workspace === workspace).map(record => record.id); }","check":{"status":"pass","findings":[{"text":"Workspace selection compares exact workspace IDs, never projectName.","status":"pass","reconsider":false,"reasons":[]}]}},{"id":"changed-database","task":"Implement solve({writers,items}) returning {database,count}. Current requirement explicitly replaces the old deployment assumption: when writers>1 use postgres, otherwise sqlite. Count unique string items. The earlier decision must not override this new requirement.","context":{"text":"Use sqlite for this deployment.","rationale":"The deployment has one writer; operational simplicity was preferred.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[{"field":"writers","operator":"eq","value":1,"explanation":"The deployment has exactly one writer."}],"checks":[{"field":"database","operator":"eq","value":"sqlite","explanation":"Use sqlite for this deployment."}]},"code":"function solve({writers,items}) { return {database: writers > 1 ? 'postgres' : 'sqlite', count: new Set(items.filter(item => typeof item === 'string')).size}; }","check":{"status":"unknown","findings":[{"text":"Use sqlite for this deployment.","status":"unknown","reconsider":true,"reasons":["Assumption changed: The deployment has exactly one writer."]}]}},{"id":"russian-attachment","task":"Реализуй solve({files}): верни массив объектов {name,storage} для файлов с расширением .txt (без учёта регистра), сохраняя порядок. Место хранения определяется ранее согласованным решением. Вход files — массив строк.","context":{"text":"Customer attachment storage must be device-only.","rationale":"Attachments have only local-processing consent.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"storage","operator":"eq","value":"device-only","explanation":"Customer attachment storage must be device-only."}]},"code":"function solve({files}) { return files.filter(name => /\\.txt$/i.test(name)).map(name => ({name, storage: 'device-only'})); }","check":{"status":"pass","findings":[{"text":"Customer attachment storage must be device-only.","status":"pass","reconsider":false,"reasons":[]}]}},{"id":"changed-retention","task":"Implement solve({agesDays}) returning {kept,retentionDays}. The user has now explicitly changed retention to 30 days, replacing the old decision. Keep ages 0 through 30 inclusive in input order. Inputs are finite numbers.","context":{"text":"Retention is seven days.","rationale":"The old support agreement permitted seven days of logs.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"retentionDays","operator":"eq","value":7,"explanation":"Retention is seven days."}]},"code":"function solve({agesDays}) { return {kept: agesDays.filter(age => age >= 0 && age <= 30), retentionDays: 30}; }","check":{"status":"conflict","findings":[{"text":"Retention is seven days.","status":"conflict","reconsider":false,"reasons":["Retention is seven days."]}]}},{"id":"transcript-jobs","task":"Implement solve({ids}) returning one job per nonempty string ID, deduplicated in first-seen order. Each job is {id, engine, destination}. Engine is whisper. Recover the approved processing choice from project context.","context":{"text":"Transcript job destination must be local.","rationale":"Customers consented only to local processing.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"destination","operator":"eq","value":"local","explanation":"Transcript job destination must be local."}]},"code":"function solve({ids}) { return [...new Set(ids.filter(id => typeof id === 'string' && id.length > 0))].map(id => ({id, engine: 'whisper', destination: 'local'})); }","check":{"status":"pass","findings":[{"text":"Transcript job destination must be local.","status":"pass","reconsider":false,"reasons":[]}]}},{"id":"retry-policy","task":"Implement solve({method,status,attempt}) returning {retry:boolean,delayMs:number}. attempt is completed attempts, starting at 1. GET may retry 429 or 500..599 while attempt<3, with delay 100*2**(attempt-1); otherwise delay is 0. Apply the previously approved write-method restriction. Methods are uppercase HTTP verbs.","context":{"text":"POST requests must never be retried automatically.","rationale":"Duplicate writes have caused duplicate charges; there is no idempotency contract.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"postRetry","operator":"eq","value":false,"explanation":"POST requests must never be retried automatically."}]},"code":"function solve({method,status,attempt}) { const retry = method === 'GET' && (status === 429 || (status >= 500 && status <= 599)) && attempt < 3; return {retry, delayMs: retry ? 100 * 2 ** (attempt - 1) : 0}; }","check":{"status":"pass","findings":[{"text":"POST requests must never be retried automatically.","status":"pass","reconsider":false,"reasons":[]}]}},{"id":"event-export","task":"Implement solve({events}) as an event export: retain each event with a string id; output id and type (default unknown), preserving order. Apply the approved personal-data rule to any other fields. Do not mutate input.","context":{"text":"Export only id and type; never include email, token, text, or other fields.","rationale":"Exports are shared for aggregate troubleshooting and must exclude private content.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"hasPrivateFields","operator":"eq","value":false,"explanation":"Export only id and type; never include email, token, text, or other fields."}]},"code":"function solve({events}) { return events.filter(event => event !== null && typeof event === 'object' && typeof event.id === 'string').map(event => ({id: event.id, type: event.type ?? 'unknown'})); }","check":{"status":"pass","findings":[{"text":"Export only id and type; never include email, token, text, or other fields.","status":"pass","reconsider":false,"reasons":[]}]}},{"id":"money-parser","task":"Implement solve({amounts}) returning the summed monetary amount in the approved unit. Inputs are nonnegative decimal strings, zero to two fraction digits, up to 1000000.00. Leading zeros are valid. Return {total,unit}. Avoid binary floating point rounding errors.","context":{"text":"Money totals are integers in cents, with unit cents.","rationale":"Downstream ledger APIs expect integer minor units.","alternatives":[],"owner":"Synthetic fixture owner","assumptions":[],"checks":[{"field":"unit","operator":"eq","value":"cents","explanation":"Money totals are integers in cents, with unit cents."}]},"code":"function solve({amounts}) { let total = 0; for (const amount of amounts) { const [whole, fraction = ''] = amount.split('.'); total += Number(whole) * 100 + Number(fraction.padEnd(2, '0')); } return {total, unit: 'cents'}; }","check":{"status":"pass","findings":[{"text":"Money totals are integers in cents, with unit cents.","status":"pass","reconsider":false,"reasons":[]}]}}]}
